<title>UK: Uk's Clarke says to raise insurance premium tax.</title>
<headline>Uk's Clarke says to raise insurance premium tax.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chancellor of the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke said he would increase UK insurance premium tax to four percent from 2.5 percent.</p>
<p>&quot;I propose to increase insurance premium tax, which applies top most general insurance, to four per cent,&quot; Clarke told Parliament in his budget speech for 1997.8.</p>
<p>&quot;Three quarters of all insurance -- including life and other long-term insurance -- will remain exempt. Insurance remains undertaxed for consumers compared with other services in this country,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717.</p>
</text>
